# A copy of Political Triumph copies its abilities but not its counters (CR 707.2, 122.1): Bot2 casts Fractured Identity on
# Bot1's enchantment, which has two plan counters. The original is exiled and Bot2 gets a token copy with none. The copy's
# abilities are Bot2's now: Bot2's Ornithopter entering makes Bot2 scry 1 (keeping the Island) and puts the copy's first
# plan counter on it, while Bot1's Ornithopter entering afterwards does nothing - Bot1 controls no Political Triumph.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Political Triumph
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Fractured Identity
Ornithopter
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Political Triumph.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Plains |)
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Plains |)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Political Triumph.Counters.Plan = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fractured Identity.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Political Triumph)
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Arrange(Island |)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Political Triumph
Bot2.Battlefield.Political Triumph.Token = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Political Triumph.Counters.Plan = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
